<main id="main"><div class="container"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="index.html">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page"><span>Conventional Mortgage Loans in Miami</span></li></ol></nav></div><section class="hero"><div class="container hero-grid"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Conventional financing</p><h1>Conventional Mortgage Loans in Miami</h1><p>Compare conventional loan options for Miami homes, condos, second homes, investment properties, and refinances.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="start.html">Compare Conventional Options</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="mortgage-calculator-florida.html">Get a Quote</a></div><div class="trust-row"><span class="trust-pill">Matthew Gromadzki</span><span class="trust-pill">NMLS #2560919</span><span class="trust-pill">Miami · Florida</span><span class="trust-pill">Call (305) 988-4806</span></div></div><div class="hero-panel rate-card"><div class="rate-item"><span>Best first step</span><strong>Preapproval</strong></div><div class="rate-item"><span>Core review</span><strong>Payment + cash to close</strong></div><div class="rate-item"><span>Miami focus</span><strong>Condo + jumbo checks</strong></div><a class="btn btn-primary full" href="start.html">Send Scenario</a></div></div></section><section class="section"><div class="container two-col"><article class="prose"><p>Conventional mortgages are often a strong fit for Miami buyers with solid credit, stable income, and enough funds for down payment and closing costs. They can be used for primary homes, second homes, condos, and investment properties.</p><p>Because Miami property types vary widely, the best conventional option depends on the property, occupancy, loan amount, down payment, and overall borrower profile.</p><h2>When conventional financing makes sense</h2><p>Conventional financing may offer competitive pricing and flexible terms when the borrower and property meet agency guidelines. It can also be useful when comparing mortgage insurance costs against FHA.</p><p>The loan structure should be reviewed carefully for condos, higher loan amounts, gift funds, self-employed income, and investment property scenarios.</p><h2>Miami property types to review closely</h2><p>Condos, townhomes, multi-unit properties, second homes, and investment properties may require additional review. Condo project documentation and insurance coverage can be just as important as borrower income and credit.</p><p>A mortgage quote should include estimated principal and interest, taxes, insurance, association dues, mortgage insurance where applicable, and cash to close.</p></article><aside><form class="lead-form lead-form-compact" method="post" action="quote.html" data-lead-form><h2>Request a Conventional Mortgage Loans Miami Quote</h2><p>Answer a few basics and we’ll review the best mortgage path for your scenario.</p><input type="hidden" name="source_page" value="preview"><label>Loan goal<select name="loan_goal" required><option value="">Select one</option><option>Buying a home</option><option>Refinancing</option><option>Cash-out refinance</option><option>Investment property</option><option>Condo financing</option></select></label><div class="form-row"><label>Purchase price / value<input name="property_value" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="$650,000"></label><label>Down payment / equity<input name="down_payment" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="$100,000"></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Credit score range<select name="credit_score"><option value="">Select range</option><option>760+</option><option>720–759</option><option>680–719</option><option>640–679</option><option>Below 640</option><option>Not sure</option></select></label><label>Property city<input name="property_city" placeholder="Miami"></label></div><div class="form-row"><label>Name<input name="name" autocomplete="name" required></label><label>Phone<input name="phone" autocomplete="tel" required></label></div><label>Email<input name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required></label><button class="btn btn-primary full" type="submit">Start Mortgage Review</button><p class="form-note">No obligation. Mortgage options depend on underwriting, lender guidelines, property type, and documentation.</p></form></aside></div></section><section class="section soft"><div class="container"><div class="cta-band"><div><p class="eyebrow">Fast next step</p><h2>Get a mortgage scenario review before you make a decision.</h2><p>Send purchase price, down payment, credit range, income type, and property city. The goal is to compare real options, not guess based on generic rates.</p></div><div class="hero-actions"><a class="btn btn-primary" href="start.html">Start Review</a><a class="btn btn-secondary" href="tel:+13059884806">Call (305) 988-4806</a></div></div></div></section><section class="section faq-section"><div class="container narrow"><p class="eyebrow">Questions</p><h2>Conventional Mortgage Loans in Miami FAQ</h2><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Is conventional better than FHA?</summary><p>It depends on credit score, down payment, mortgage insurance, property type, and total monthly payment. Many buyers should compare both before deciding.</p></details><details><summary>Can conventional loans be used for condos?</summary><p>Yes, but the condo project may need to meet specific guidelines. Building-level review can affect approval.</p></details><details><summary>Can I use conventional financing for an investment property?</summary><p>Yes. Investment property financing is common, but down payment, reserves, rate, and documentation requirements may differ from a primary residence.</p></details></div></div></section><section class="section related-section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Keep comparing</p><h2>Related mortgage pages</h2><div class="card-grid small-grid"><a class="mini-card" href="fha-loan-miami.html">FHA Loans Miami<span>→</span></a><a class="mini-card" href="jumbo-loans-miami.html">Jumbo Loans Miami<span>→</span></a><a class="mini-card" href="investment-property-loans-miami.html">Investment Property Loans Miami<span>→</span></a><a class="mini-card" href="mortgage-broker-miami.html">Mortgage Broker Miami<span>→</span></a></div></div></section></main>
